# Line endings are part of the protocol here: the BIP39 wordlist is hashed
# against the official SHA-256, and the skill and plugin files are embedded
# into the binary byte for byte. A CRLF checkout would ship a wallet that
# derives the wrong keys. Everything text stays LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# CRLF bytes are this fixture's subject, and its checksum and test depend on
# them; text=auto would normalize them to LF on the next `git add`.
testdata/fixtures/sse/crlf_endings.sse -text
*.png binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
